Z||000000||Eric||12-17-1999||06:41 PM||||I've got almost 200 miles on my 3.1 and I have to say it is really pickin' up the pace.  I complained about a lack of torque and power, but I hadn't taken it over 4000 rpm. because I wanted to be easy on it.  Well I've still managed to stay below 4000 rpm, but it hasn't been easy.  That thing wants to pull like crazy.  I can't wait till I get my new fuel pressure regulator and put a few more miles on it, so I can really let it fly.  <P>Today I was driving down the road when all of the sudden as I was accelerating in second gear, I heard a pop and the whole engine seemed to get louder by twenty decibels.  I pulled over to see if any thing had come apart like the exhaust manifold, when I noticed some hot air escaping from the front y-pipe collector and the smell of exaust fumes out of the engine compartment.  I blew a hole in the y-pipe!  Oh well, guess I need one of Stroker's turbo kits so I can replace the damaged part.  Anyone want the leftover turbo?||||reg||10
